I apply commits from the list, but I don't want to have to respond to
them to say they've been applied.

Probably we can detect when patches have been applied, and respond with
the specific SHA they've been applied as. This mirrors the FreeBSD
practice of updating PRs with a message like "a commit in main
references this bug."

Is this something we can do deterministically and/or with inference? I
would prefer to not have to reference the message ID in every commit I
make.

The goal is to clearly indicate on the list which patches have been
committed, so I can take them out of the review queue automatically.
